<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/6th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Bi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">597 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century-bce">6th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Bi was fought in 597 BCE near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-zhuang-of-chu">King Zhuang of Chu</a> defeated an army of Jin that had come to relieve the State of Zheng. The victory, described in the Zuo zhuan, made Chu the leading power of the central plain for a time and gave King Zhuang his place among the hegemons of the Spring and Autumn period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bi.jpg" alt="Battle of Bi" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Bi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
